            <ArticleTitle>Regioselective Synthesis of o-Benzenediboronic Acids via Ir-Catalyzed o-C-H Borylation Directed by a Pyrazolylaniline-Modified Boronyl Group.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>886-889</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b00041</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ir-catalyzed ortho-directed C-H borylation of pyrazolylaniline (PZA)-modified arylboronic acids with bis(pinacolate)diboron afforded o-benzenediboronic acids in which two boronyl groups are differentially modified by pinacol (PIN) and PZA. By using this borylation after nondirected Ir-catalyzed C-H borylation, o-benzenediboronic acids are conveniently synthesized from unfunctionalized arenes. The differentially modified o-benzenediboronic acids undergo selective oxidation and Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling at the PZA-modified boronyl groups, affording o-functionalized arylboronic acids selectively.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
